=== day
n: 6
title: Lists of shows
subtitle: Arrays, objects, loops
hours: 3 hours
page: index.html
slot: js | js | app.js
file: app.js = js
refs: data.js, @page, page.js

--- intro
A real app doesn't show one show: it shows lists. Today you learn how JavaScript keeps many values together (**arrays**), how it describes one thing with named values (**objects**), and how to go through a whole list with a **loop**.

The file **data.js** (a read-only tab above the code box) holds twelve shows, each one an object with a name, genres, a rating and more. You start in the Console, exploring the data. Then you write small functions that pick shows from the list: the best ones, one by its id, the ones that match a search, the ones in a genre.

As before, a helper file, **page.js**, uses your functions to fill in the page. It also scrolls the preview to the newest part you've made.

